-- More countries (todos.txt Q2): routine schedules for 17 more countries,
-- so families there get the right visits and reminders.
--
-- Same rules as 20261001000001_countries.sql: each country's national
-- programme for ALL babies, birth to about 6 years; earliest recommended age
-- where the source gives a range; no seasonal (flu, COVID), RSV, risk-group,
-- regional or travel vaccines (RSV and flu are optional reminders in the
-- app, lib/core/optional_vaccines.dart). Left out on purpose: rotavirus
-- dose 3 that only applies with the 3-dose brand (DE, ES, FR); NL's extra
-- 6-week 6-in-1 for babies whose mothers weren't vaccinated in pregnancy.
-- All unverified until a pediatrician checks them (todos.txt 21).
--
-- Sources, checked 27 Oct 2026 (with the WHO/UNICEF 2025 schedule data,
-- published 3 Jun 2026, as a cross-check):
-- IN: MoHFW Universal Immunisation Programme (PCV national since 2021, fIPV
--     dose 3 at 9 months since 2023). JE is district-only: left out.
-- BD: DGHS EPI; typhoid conjugate at 15 months from 1 Aug 2026.
-- QA: MOPH national programme as reported to WHO (2025).
-- KW: MOH ministerial decision 2024 / WHO 2025 (MMRV at 2 years, DTaP at 3.5).
-- OM: MOH EPI as reported to WHO (2025); DT at school entry (6 years).
-- BH: MOH immunisation schedule page and 2025 PDF. BCG is only for babies of
--     parents from TB-endemic countries (Pakistan is one): ask your clinic.
-- MY: KKM National Immunisation Programme / WHO 2025.
-- AU: National Immunisation Program (NSW Health Oct 2026, NCIRS Aug 2026);
--     first visit "2 months, can be given from 6 weeks".
-- DE: STIKO Epidemiologisches Bulletin 4/2026 (MenC dropped in 2026).
-- IE: HSE primary schedule for babies born from 1 Oct 2024.
-- IT: PNPV 2023-2025 (extended to the end of 2026); regions may add more.
-- ES: CISNS calendario común 2026 (approved 12 Dec 2025).
-- FR: Calendrier des vaccinations 2026 (July 2026).
-- NL: RIVM Rijksvaccinatieprogramma 2026 (2025 changes: booster at 12
--     months, MMR 2 at 3 years, DTaP at 5).
-- NO: FHI barnevaksinasjonsprogrammet 2026 (DTaP-IPV is at ~7, left out).
-- SE: Folkhälsomyndigheten 2026; chickenpox at 18 months from 1 Jan 2027.
-- TR: Ministry of Health childhood schedule 2026 (6-in-1 at 2/4/6/18 months
--     since Apr 2025, chickenpox dose 2 at 4 years from Sep 2026).
